course: dictionary
lesson: 12966
title: Exemplary: very good, a model for others
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Maya's behaviour in class was exemplary, so her teacher praised her.» Look at the clues: the teacher praised her, so exemplary must be something good. Try a meaning in the sentence: "Maya's behaviour in class was very good, so her teacher praised her." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Exemplary means so good that it is an example for others to copy. A pupil who helps others, works hard and is kind to everyone can be called an exemplary pupil. The word is about being a model, not just being good at one thing.
explain: Adults also use exemplary in a more formal way. «The judge gave an exemplary punishment to warn others.» Here exemplary means a punishment that serves as a warning, so that other people do not do the same thing. The same word can mean "a good example" or "a warning example", so the rest of the sentence tells you which one.
fact: Exemplary means very good, so good that others can copy it.
fact: «Exemplary behaviour» means behaviour that is an excellent example for everyone.
fact: In school reports, teachers write exemplary to praise excellent work or behaviour.
fact: In a formal sense, exemplary can mean serving as a warning or example, as in «an exemplary punishment».
fact: Excellent and model are close in meaning to exemplary when it praises someone's behaviour.
exercise: «Maya's behaviour in class was exemplary, so her teacher praised her.» What does exemplary mean? | Noisy and silly | Very small | Late for school | *Very good, so good that others can copy
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to exemplary? | Careless | Lost | *Excellent | Quiet
exercise: «The judge gave an exemplary punishment to warn others.» What does exemplary mean in this sentence? | A punishment that was forgotten | *A punishment that serves as a warning to others | A prize for winning | A punishment that was kind and gentle
test: Which phrase has the same meaning as «an exemplary pupil»? | A pupil who has lost all of their books | A pupil who sits at the back | *A pupil who works hard and sets a good example | A pupil who is always late
test: Why might a teacher write «exemplary» in a school report? | To say the child lost a game | To say the report is too long | *To praise excellent work or behaviour | To say the child must leave school
exam: Which word best replaces exemplary in «The exemplary pupil helped everyone.»? | *Excellent | Noisy | Tired | Careless
